<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Six Arrows</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Altı Ok</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Six Arrows are the symbol and flag of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kemalism">Kemalism</a>, the ideology of the Turkish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republican-peoples-party">Republican People's Party</a> (CHP), each arrow standing for one of its fundamental pillars: republicanism, populism, nationalism, laicism, statism and reformism. The arrows are believed to have been conceived by İsmail Hakkı Tonguç, a Turkish scientist who made significant contributions to the Turkish education system. The principles of the Six Arrows were added to the Turkish Constitution on 5 February 1937, and from August 1938 the flag was hoisted at all official buildings. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republicanism">Republicanism</a>, the party's main idea, holds that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> belongs to the people.</p></div>
